ilable to sync course progress. Every notebook can run in the browser through Pyodide, while heavier workloads such as fine-tuning and large-model inference may require additional compute or external services such as Google Colab or Kaggle.","limits_fr":"Le programme est accessible gratuitement sans compte ni carte bancaire. Une connexion facultative avec Google ou GitHub permet de synchroniser la progression du cours. Chaque notebook peut être exécuté dans le navigateur avec Pyodide, tandis que les tâches plus lourdes comme le fine-tuning et l’inférence de grands modèles peuvent nécessiter des ressources de calcul supplémentaires ou des services externes tels que Google Colab ou Kaggle.","caveats":["An account is optional for learning but can be used to sync course progress with Google or GitHub.","Some advanced notebooks require additional compute and may use external services such as Google Colab or Kaggle.","The curriculum is actively evolving and some later phases are still being developed."],"caveats_fr":["Un compte est facultatif pour apprendre, mais peut être utilisé pour synchroniser la progression du cours avec Google ou GitHub.","Certains notebooks avancés nécessitent des ressources de calcul supplémentaires et peuvent utiliser des services externes comme Google Colab ou Kaggle.","Le programme évolue encore et certaines phases avancées sont toujours en cours de développement."],"tags":["course","ai","machine-learning","llm","rag","ai-agents","python","open-source"],"source":{"url":"https://github.com/PavanMudigonda/zero-to-ai","type":"official-repository","official":true},"last_verified":"2026-08-16","status":"active","confidence":"high"}}]$records$::jsonb) as x(
  source_key text, source_record_id text, name text, slug text,
  canonical_slug text, website_url text, category text, pricing_model text,
  is_free boolean, last_verified text, raw_data jsonb
)
on conflict (site_id, source_key, source_record_id) do update set
  name=excluded.name, slug=excluded.slug, canonical_slug=excluded.canonical_slug,
  website_url=excluded.website_url, category=excluded.category,
  pricing_model=excluded.pricing_model, is_free=excluded.is_free,
  last_verified=excluded.last_verified, raw_data=excluded.raw_data,
  match_method=excluded.match_method, imported_at=excluded.imported_at;

update catalog_source_records r set tool_id=t.id,
  match_method=case when r.source_key='autoventure' and t.source_dataset='autoventure'
    then 'new-canonical' else r.match_method end
from tool_catalog t
where r.site_id=t.site_id and r.canonical_slug=t.slug and r.site_id='7635559c-2c64-4d76-8b3b-1c69e4a412f8';

insert into tool_sources (site_id, tool_id, source_type, url, label, retrieved_at, reliability)
select r.site_id, r.tool_id, 'dataset', s.url, s.name || ' (' || s.license || ')',
  r.imported_at, s.trust_score
from catalog_source_records r join catalog_data_sources s on s.key=r.source_key
where r.tool_id is not null and not exists (
  select 1 from tool_sources ts
  where ts.tool_id=r.tool_id and ts.source_type='dataset' and ts.url=s.url
);

analyze catalog_source_records;
analyze tool_catalog;
